# ufw-focus allowlist. Copy to ~/.config/ufw-focus/allow.list and edit.
#
# One website per line. Blank lines and anything after # are ignored.
# Write the bare name: `wikipedia.org`. A pasted URL also works; the
# https:// and the /path part are stripped.
#
# Each name is also tried with `www.` in front, so `wikipedia.org` covers
# `www.wikipedia.org` too. Other subdomains are NOT covered: the firewall
# only sees numbers (IP addresses), not names, so `*.wikipedia.org` cannot
# work. List each one you need, e.g. `en.wikipedia.org`, `upload.wikimedia.org`.
#
# Big sites load pieces from other names. If a page half-loads, open the
# browser's dev tools (F12) -> Network tab, see which names fail, add them.
#
# After editing, run `ufw-focus` again to apply the new list.
#
# Examples (remove the # to use):
# en.wikipedia.org
# upload.wikimedia.org
# github.com
# api.anthropic.com      # Claude Code
# claude.ai
